Source: zyphoros-installer
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: zyphoros-installer
Architecture: all
Depends: calamares,
# The password check (libpwquality) fails every password without cracklib's
# dictionary, which libcrack2 only recommends.
         cracklib-runtime,
# Partitioning and copying the system: mkfs.fat for the EFI partition
# (udisks2 only recommends dosfstools), unsquashfs for unpackfs (Calamares
# only recommends squashfs-tools).
         dosfstools,
         squashfs-tools,
         zyphoros-branding,
         rsync,
         cryptsetup,
         keyutils,
         pkexec,
         sudo,
         x11-xserver-utils,
         xdg-user-dirs,
         libglib2.0-bin,
         qml-module-qtquick-window2,
         qml-module-qtquick2,
         ${misc:Depends}
Conflicts: calamares-settings-debian
Description: Zyphor OS installer (live image only)
 Settings and branding for the Calamares installer on Zyphor OS's live
 image, based on Debian's calamares-settings-debian: "Install Zyphor OS" in
 the menu and on the live desktop, GRUB for UEFI (Secure Boot) or BIOS
 installed from the ISO without a network, and the login screen of the
 installed system set up (with optional autologin).
 .
 The installer removes this package, Calamares and the live system
 packages from the installed system.
